                      (vel1/cmds/asm.asm):00732         * Mnemonic words are high bit terminated
                      (vel1/cmds/asm.asm):00733         * First numeric byte is the base opcode (before addressing modes considered)
                      (vel1/cmds/asm.asm):00734         * 2nd is flags:
                      (vel1/cmds/asm.asm):00735         * Least significiant 4 bits = index into handler table
                      (vel1/cmds/asm.asm):00736         * 0= LBRA & LBSR (non comparitive long branches/no pre-byte)
                      (vel1/cmds/asm.asm):00737         * 1= Immediate (no register options) ex. ORCC
                      (vel1/cmds/asm.asm):00738         * 2= 16 bit register commands
                      (vel1/cmds/asm.asm):00739         * 3= 8 bit register commands
                      (vel1/cmds/asm.asm):00740         * 4= CLR, etc. Inherent (A,B,D,E,F,W all supported)
                      (vel1/cmds/asm.asm):00741         * 5= 'Fixed' (register not negotiable) inherent commands
                      (vel1/cmds/asm.asm):00742         * 6= LEAx - Indexed only
                      (vel1/cmds/asm.asm):00743         * 7= Register to register (TFR,EXG) (now patched for dual size 0 register)
                      (vel1/cmds/asm.asm):00744         * 8= Stack push/pull (except for W - it's done as type 5)
                      (vel1/cmds/asm.asm):00745         * 9= 16 bit Relative comparative branches setup flag
                      (vel1/cmds/asm.asm):00746         * A= 8 bit Relative comparative branches
                      (vel1/cmds/asm.asm):00747         * B= Pseudo op
